      "message": "minor:\n\u003e A non-present pte means that the MMIO page has not been lazily mapped in the host MMU yet. \n\n\"lazily\" here seems a bit confusing, s/lazily/yet/ ? Or to make the intent clear, something like:\n```\n/*\n * At this point(during pKVM init), all MMIO pages are still owned by\n * the host. A non-present pte simply means the page is not mapped in\n * the host MMU; it will be mapped on demand on the first host access\n * (see pkvm_handle_host_ept_violation()), or annotated later if the\n * pages are donated to hyp (e.g. IOMMU MMIO, see hyp_iommu_init()).\n * Either way its state (PKVM_PAGE_OWNED, PKVM_ID_HOST) is already\n * effectively set, since the pte is zeroed.\n */\n```",
